# =============================================================================
#  Decay of an mRNA molecule count        A --k_deg--> 0
# =============================================================================
#  After transcription is shut off, a pool of N0 mRNA molecules degrades
#  first-order:
#
#        dA/dt = -k_deg * A       ->       A(t) = N0 * exp(-k_deg * t)
#
#  This is the kind of experiment single-molecule methods (e.g. smFISH) produce:
#  at each time point you COUNT molecules, so the data are non-negative integers,
#  and biological/technical variation makes them OVER-DISPERSED (their scatter is
#  wider than a Poisson's). The starting count N0 is pinned by the early points and
#  the rate k_deg by the slope of the (log) decay, so a single count time course
#  identifies both -- provided you score the counts with a COUNT likelihood rather
#  than least squares (see mrna_decay_neg_bin.conf).
#
#  No `begin actions` block: the time course comes from the `experiment:` line.
# =============================================================================

begin model

  begin parameters
    k_deg   0.3     # degradation rate     [1 / time]        <- FITTED
    N0      200     # initial mRNA count   [molecules]       <- FITTED
  end parameters

  begin molecule types
    A()
  end molecule types

  begin seed species
    A()  N0           # start from N0 molecules
  end seed species

  begin observables
    Molecules  Obs_A  A()      # a molecule COUNT (the data are integer counts of this)
  end observables

  begin reaction rules
    death: A() -> 0    k_deg
  end reaction rules

end model
